.TH APKSYNC 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
apksync \- repository synchronisation to publication mirrors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apksync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apksync
synchronises the local generation repositories outward to the
publication target with rsync (archive, compress, delayed updates).
.PP
The mirror converges exactly to the published set:
.I .apk
payloads,
.I APKINDEX.tar.gz
and
.I Packages.adb
indexes, and
.I keys/*.pub
trust keys (key sync preserves the status quo; drop the rule if key
distribution is handled elsewhere).
Everything else on the mirror is deleted:
stale withdrawn NVRs, builder fossils
(gen-root
.IR repository.db ,
.IR compact.sh ,
per-arch
.IR repository.db
files), migration evidence, journals and
.I *.sh
helpers.
.I aarch64
and
.I noarch
subdirectories sync like any other directory:
traversal is by directory, selection is by filename.
.PP
Deletion is guarded, never blind: preflight refuses the run unless
both generation indexes exist and the source holds at least 1000
APKs, so an empty or half-mounted source can never wipe the mirror.
Preview any first run with rsync
.I -n
(dry run) using the same filter set and review the
.I *deleting
lines before the real run.
.PP
In-flight
.I *.publishing-*
temporaries and the local
.I ownership.json
migration evidence are excluded by the same rule and never leave the host.
.PP
Configuration comes from
.IR /etc/saphira/apksync.conf :
.I SAPHIRA_REPO_DIR
(the local source) and
.I SAPHIRA_SYNC_TARGET
(the mirror destination) are both required. Takes no arguments and
publishes nothing by itself; run it after
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
then
.I apk update
on consumers.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/saphira/apksync.conf
Source and target configuration (both required).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Synchronised.
.TP
.B 1
Missing configuration or rsync failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
sudo sign-apk-repo && sudo apksync && apk update
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira (7),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR installpkg (8),
.BR saphira-build (8)
